From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a two-finger flick on a page keeps gliding

libinput reports a scroll stop when the fingers lift and leaves momentum
to whoever draws the content. Native clients run their own; a page on a
tty got nothing and stopped dead.

- `FlingTracker` (`ui/events/ozone/evdev/domicile/`) measures the speed
  over the last 100 ms before the lift. Fingers resting 100 ms before
  lifting give no fling.
- At a finger stop, the converter dispatches `kScrollFlingStart` at that
  speed, after the stop native clients need. The browser runs its own
  fling curve, as for a Wayland touchpad.
- The speed is the fingers' own: libinput's distance times the scroll
  factor, as native clients get it. `ScrollAccelerator` still speeds up a
  fast drag, but the glide does not carry its gain on.
- Fingers resting on the pad (libinput 1.19's hold gesture, which the
  machine's libinput sends though the sysroot's header lacks it) or
  scrolling again dispatch `kScrollFlingCancel`, catching the page.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
